 "result_text": "I added the issue's size optimization to `gif.save` in `gif.py`, and it's on by default for overlapping frames. I only ran a quick smoke test: a 5-frame matplotlib animation saved to a GIF with 5 frames. I didn't measure file size against the old output or run the test suite.\n\nWhen `overlapping=True` and there is more than one frame, `save` now does this:\n- **Shared palette:** it quantizes all frames together to 255 colors, without dithering.\n- **Unchanged pixels:** it turns any pixel that matches the previous frame transparent, using palette index 0, so each frame only stores what changed.\n- **Non-overlapping or single frame:** the old code path is unchanged.\n\nFrames are converted to RGB first, so any alpha channel in the PNGs is dropped.\n\nAs the issue notes, this is slower and uses more memory than before. I used numpy, which matplotlib already depends on, so there are no new dependencies.",
